From 53ccc4b69582eb90e9aaa7d4c150776002b74285 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:39:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/43] pvr: plumb sync values through the winsys submit API
 (step 1 of 3, behaviour-preserving)

Groundwork for timeline syncobjs, which is what removes the queue's per-job sync
create/destroy (~250 DRM ioctls per Xwayland frame, ~80% of it this path).

The winsys submit API carried bare struct vk_sync pointers, so a timeline point could not be
expressed: pvr_drm_job_render.c hardcoded .value = 0 at 10 sites and asserted
!(sync->flags & VK_SYNC_IS_TIMELINE) at 8. Mesa already has the value-carrying types and the
null-job path already uses them, so this change adopts them everywhere:

  pvr_winsys.h      4x 'struct vk_sync *wait'      -> 'struct vk_sync_wait wait'
                    3x 'struct vk_sync *signal_sync*' -> 'const struct vk_sync_signal *'
  pvr_arch_job_{render,compute,transfer}.c and pvr_job_{render,compute,transfer}.h
                    wrappers, ws_submit_info_init helpers and state-init helpers take/forward
                    the new types
  powervr + pvrsrvkm job implementations consume wait.sync / signal->sync
  pvr_arch_queue.c  call sites wrap the bare syncs in the value-carrying structs

**Values are all still zero, so this is behaviour-preserving**: a binary syncobj is defined to
use value 0, which is what the code passed before. No functional change is intended or observed.

Verified: build clean; bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize, samplers, storageimages, mrt, varyings,
inatt, ubos, stgbuf, vattrib all PASS; glmark2 --validate 27/0.

Next (step 2): the queue keeps a persistent timeline sync per job type and increments its point,
so no sync object is created or destroyed per job.
